/E (The Department of Electrical & Electronics Engineering organized SAMAGRA-2026 on 5 March 2026, with Renewable Energy as its theme. The event featured a Technical Presentation  and Project Expo, providing students a platform to showcase their knowledge, creativity, and innovative ideas in solar energy, wind power, energy storage, and smart grids. A total of  39 teams actively participated, presenting insightful concepts and working prototypes focused on sustainable energy solutions. The projects and presentations were evaluated by expert faculty and judges based on innovation, technical knowledge, presentation quality, and practical applicability. The event successfully promoted innovation, sustainability, and hands-on learning among students.)
